## 1. Start evidence capture and verify the native host

Save this prompt and its companion `windows-tester-prompt.json` in one directory,
open PowerShell 7 or Windows PowerShell 5.1 there, and run:

```powershell
$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
$Evidence = Join-Path $PWD 'windows-evidence'
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $Evidence | Out-Null
Start-Transcript -Path (Join-Path $Evidence 'transcript.txt') -Force

$Binding = Get-Content -LiteralPath '.\windows-tester-prompt.json' -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json
$HostEvidence = [ordered]@{
  os = [Environment]::OSVersion.VersionString
  processorArchitecture = $env:PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE
  nodeVersion = (& node --version)
  nodePlatform = (& node -p 'process.platform')
  nodeArchitecture = (& node -p 'process.arch')
  powershell = $PSVersionTable.PSVersion.ToString()
}
$HostEvidence | ConvertTo-Json | Set-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $Evidence 'host.json') -Encoding utf8
if ($HostEvidence.nodePlatform -ne 'win32' -or $HostEvidence.nodeArchitecture -ne 'x64') {
  throw 'Native Windows x64 Node.js is required'
}
if ([int]((& node -p 'process.versions.node.split(`.`)[0]')) -lt 22) {
  throw 'Node.js 22 or later is required'
}
```

Do not change execution policy to make the test pass. Report an execution-policy
restriction as `NotRun` with a separate `Blocked` reason.

## 2. Download and verify before extraction

```powershell
$Work = Join-Path $env:TEMP 'AI SDLC Framework Windows Test'
Remove-Item -LiteralPath $Work -Recurse -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $Work | Out-Null

$Descriptor = Join-Path $Work 'release-descriptor.json'
$Checksums = Join-Path $Work 'SHA256SUMS'
$Archive = Join-Path $Work $Binding.archive.filename
Invoke-WebRequest -Uri $Binding.urls.descriptor -OutFile $Descriptor
Invoke-WebRequest -Uri $Binding.urls.checksums -OutFile $Checksums
Invoke-WebRequest -Uri $Binding.urls.archive -OutFile $Archive

function Assert-Sha256([string]$Path, [string]$Expected) {
  $Actual = (Get-FileHash -LiteralPath $Path -Algorithm SHA256).Hash.ToLowerInvariant()
  if ($Actual -ne $Expected.ToLowerInvariant()) {
    throw "SHA-256 mismatch for $Path"
  }
}
Assert-Sha256 $Descriptor $Binding.identity.descriptorSha256
Assert-Sha256 $Checksums $Binding.identity.checksumsSha256
Assert-Sha256 $Archive $Binding.archive.sha256
if ((Get-Item -LiteralPath $Archive).Length -ne [int64]$Binding.archive.size) {
  throw 'Windows archive size mismatch'
}
if (-not (Select-String -LiteralPath $Checksums -SimpleMatch $Binding.archive.sha256,
    $Binding.archive.filename -Quiet)) {
  throw 'SHA256SUMS does not bind the expected Windows archive'
}
```

If the release assets are not yet public, record this phase as `NotRun` with
`Blocked: release assets unavailable`; do not substitute checkout bytes or a
mutable `latest` URL.

## 3. Isolated standalone lifecycle

Only after every download check passes:

```powershell
$Extracted = Join-Path $Work 'extracted'
Expand-Archive -LiteralPath $Archive -DestinationPath $Extracted
$Installer = Join-Path $Extracted 'install.ps1'
$TestHome = Join-Path $Work 'copilot home'
$TestChannel = Join-Path $Work 'standalone channel'
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $TestHome | Out-Null
Set-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $TestHome 'unrelated-user-file.txt') -Value 'preserve-me'

& $Installer install --channel-root $TestChannel --home $TestHome
if ($LASTEXITCODE) { throw 'Isolated install failed' }
& $Installer doctor --channel-root $TestChannel --home $TestHome |
  Tee-Object -FilePath (Join-Path $Evidence 'isolated-doctor.json')
if ($LASTEXITCODE) { throw 'Isolated doctor failed' }
& $Installer update --channel-root $TestChannel --home $TestHome
if ($LASTEXITCODE) { throw 'Isolated update failed' }
& $Installer uninstall --channel-root $TestChannel --home $TestHome
if ($LASTEXITCODE) { throw 'Isolated ordinary uninstall failed' }
if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $TestHome 'unrelated-user-file.txt'))) {
  throw 'Ordinary uninstall removed unrelated content'
}
& $Installer install --purge-existing --channel-root $TestChannel --home $TestHome
if ($LASTEXITCODE) { throw 'Isolated clean migration failed' }
& $Installer uninstall --purge --channel-root $TestChannel --home $TestHome
if ($LASTEXITCODE) { throw 'Isolated purge failed' }
if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $TestHome 'unrelated-user-file.txt'))) {
  throw 'Purge removed unrelated content'
}
```

## 4. Replace the installed private v1.2.4 generation

Close every GitHub Copilot CLI process. From the external PowerShell window:

```powershell
$CopilotHome = if ($env:COPILOT_HOME) { $env:COPILOT_HOME } else {
  Join-Path $HOME '.copilot'
}
$ActualChannel = Join-Path $env:LOCALAPPDATA 'ai-sdlc-framework'

& $Installer install --purge-existing --channel-root $ActualChannel --home $CopilotHome
if ($LASTEXITCODE) { throw 'v1.2.4 to OSS clean migration failed' }
& $Installer doctor --channel-root $ActualChannel --home $CopilotHome |
  Tee-Object -FilePath (Join-Path $Evidence 'post-migration-doctor.json')
if ($LASTEXITCODE) { throw 'Post-migration doctor failed' }
```

`--purge-existing` intentionally removes the previous framework installation and
its framework runtime state. It must preserve unrelated Copilot instructions and
other user content. Do not run it without accepting that framework-state reset.

